# Berkeley in-person outreach calendar

Standing venues and recurring series where the people on the onboarding list are physically reachable,
with location, cadence, the live calendar to check for specific dates, and which targets each connects
to. No specific dates are recorded here on purpose: they change every term, and a fabricated date wastes
a trip. Check the live calendar the morning you go. All venues cluster on the north edge of campus around
Hearst Avenue (Sutardja Dai Hall, Soda Hall, Calvin Lab) except Berkeley Way West, a few blocks south.

## The subject-matched one: foundations of computing

**Simons Institute for the Theory of Computing** — Calvin Lab, 2121 Berkeley Way (south edge, near
Berkeley Way West). The foundations-of-computing institute, open-door by design: atrium, coffee, visiting
fellows, public talks you can sit in on without an invitation. This is where to go to talk to the theory
crowd who would actually read a univalent-foundations argument, informally, with no gate. "Meet the
Fellows" talks run in Calvin Lab Room 116. Fall 2026 programs: Pseudorandomness & High-Dimensional
Expansion, and Spectral Theory Beyond Graphs.
- Live calendar: https://simons.berkeley.edu/calendar
- Walk-in: any weekday, the atrium.

## The AI-safety hub: Sutardja Dai Hall, 2594 Hearst Ave

Three open series run out of this building, and CHAI, the CITRIS/BAIR orbit, and the EECS theory people
are physically here. Catching people at the entrance in the morning is a real tactic; the seminars are
higher-yield, because people stand around before and after.

**CHAI AI Risk Speaker Series** — talks on AI risks and mitigations from academia, civil society and
industry, in Sutardja Dai Hall (rooms vary, e.g. 621). Connects to: Stuart Russell (CHAI director),
Anca Dragan (CHAI), Andrew Critch, Dylan Hadfield-Menell when visiting.
- Live calendar: https://ai-risk.berkeley.edu/speaker-series.html

**CITRIS Research Exchange** — free one-hour seminars, noon Pacific, live in the Banatao Auditorium,
310 Sutardja Dai Hall. Open to anyone. Has hosted Stuart Russell on human-compatible / ethical AI.
- Host: https://citris-uc.org/events/

**CLIMB / Voleon Seminar Series** — 310 Sutardja Dai Hall. The machine-learning / decision-theory seminar.
Ariel Procaccia (the social-choice theorist whose impossibility results are load-bearing in the field
email) gave one of these in October 2025. Connects to: the social-choice-and-alignment line (Procaccia,
Conitzer, Hadfield-Menell).
- Live calendar: https://climb.berkeley.edu/seminars

**Soda Hall** — next door, EECS and the BAIR lab. Same morning-entrance tactic; same people.

## The science-of-happiness node: Berkeley Way West, 2121 Berkeley Way

**Dacher Keltner's Social Interaction Lab** and the **Greater Good Science Center**, both of which he
directs, are housed here, along with the Psychology department offices. He is a former teacher of yours;
the warm route is an email first, then a visit, not a cold hallway catch. Walk into the lab or the Center
front desk and ask when he is in — staffed labs know their director's schedule. Verify his current-term
teaching on https://classes.berkeley.edu (search his name) before relying on any room or time.

## Annual, not walk-in

**CHAI Annual Workshop** — held at Asilomar (Pacific Grove) in early June, invitation/registration. The
one time most of the human-compatible-AI community is in one room. Worth targeting for next June.
- https://humancompatible.ai

